From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HourlySword <hourlysword.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:08:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: shorter room entries, memory that no longer creeps
 up

Room entries: a room's floor and walls are drawn into its bitmap from shapes parsed on demand under a 5 MB budget, and
45% of the parses were of shapes parsed before and dropped. Half of a parsed shape was the second copy of its edges
kept for exact hit tests (asked for twice in a whole run) and its vectors kept their growth slack: the hit-test edges
are now made only when a hit test needs them (shapeEnsureHit) and every vector is trimmed, so the budget holds about
twice as many shapes. Joining edges into paths uses a sorted array instead of a hash multimap (one allocation per
edge). On the console: ticks over 150 ms after the title 18 -> 12, over 300 ms 6 -> 2, parsing in the 7-minute play
script 4.2 -> 2.2 s; the same pictures, pixel for pixel.

Memory: lean loading kept every sprite timeline it parsed, for each kind of enemy, effect or item seen (about 10 MB
after eight floors). The timelines of sprites with no clip left (counted per sprite) and none made in the last 2
seconds are now dropped above g_timelineBudgetBytes (3 MB on the FunKey), least recently used first, and parsed again
from the same tags when needed; sprites with a sound stream are kept. Clip names given by scripts (attachMovie,
createEmptyMovieClip) are interned weakly like the automatic instance names (atomOfWeak): the game's sound function
names a clip "sz" and a counter for every sound, and those stayed for good. The heap in use over a 22-minute workload
on the PC stays at 32-35 MB instead of growing from 30 to 42; on the console the game's memory levels off at about
45 MB.

Diagnostics in the log: a "long tick" line for ticks over 150 ms (ISAAC_FUNKEY_SLOWMS) with what it was spent on, a
"memory at tick" line every 1800 ticks (ISAAC_FUNKEY_MEMEVERY), totals when the game ends. Testing:
ISAAC_FUNKEY_CENSUS (a full collection first, the heap by kind, interned strings by pattern), ISAAC_FUNKEY_NOWAIT,
ISAAC_TIMELINE_KB, ISAAC_SHAPE_KB, ISAAC_LEAF_SUB, ISAAC_LEAF_REPEAT, ISAAC_LEANREAD_LOG.
